# UI Forms

## Stack
`react-hook-form` + `zod` for all forms. shadcn/ui `Form`, `FormField`, `FormItem`, `FormLabel`, `FormControl`, `FormMessage` primitives.

## Pattern
```tsx
const schema = z.object({
  host: z.string().min(1),
  port: z.coerce.number().int().min(1).max(65535),
  database: z.string().min(1),
})

const form = useForm<z.infer<typeof schema>>({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
  defaultValues: { port: 5432 },
})

<Form {...form}>
  <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
    <FormField
      control={form.control}
      name="host"
      render={({ field }) => (
        <FormItem>
          <FormLabel>{t('sources.form.host')}</FormLabel>
          <FormControl>
            <Input {...field} />
          </FormControl>
          <FormMessage />
        </FormItem>
      )}
    />
  </form>
</Form>
```

## API error mapping
`handleApiError(error, form)` from `lib/error-handling.ts` maps field-keyed API errors to react-hook-form:
```typescript
// If error.details = { "host": "unreachable", "port": "refused" }
// → form.setError("host", { message: "unreachable" })
// → form.setError("port", { message: "refused" })
```

Non-field errors → sonner toast.

## Wizard forms
Connection wizard uses URL search params for resumability. Each step validates independently before enabling the "Next" button. Forward navigation disabled until current step's zod schema passes.

## Input components
All from shadcn/ui: `Input`, `Select`, `Checkbox`, `Switch`, `Textarea`. Never build custom input primitives.

## Labels
All labels via `t('module.form.fieldName')` — never hardcode label strings. See `i18n.mdc`.

## Disabled states
Disable the submit button while `form.formState.isSubmitting`. Show a spinner inside the button, not next to it.
